{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And now, Israel, what does HaShem your Elohim ask of you.</b> Is this a small thing? And one may answer that it refers to the verse that follows it: לשמור את מצות ה׳ וגו׳ לטוב לך — that is, He does not ask this thing of you except לטוב לך, for your benefit and to multiply your reward. However, our Rabbis asked thus and answered that relative to Moses this is a minor matter, and from here our Rabbis derived that one is obligated to recite one hundred blessings every day, as it is written: מה — do not read מה but rather מאה, that is, one hundred blessings — HaShem your Elohim asks of you. And the matter can be strengthened: מה by exchanging alef-tav with bet-shin becomes יץ, which equals one hundred. And likewise in this verse there are one hundred letters minus one, and when you add one letter to make it one hundred, the calculation reaches one hundred. Some say that David instituted them, for every day one hundred people of Israel were dying. They came and told David. He arose and instituted one hundred blessings every day, as it is said: נאם הגבר הוקם על — על in gematria is one hundred, and immediately the plague was halted. Further, one can prove one hundred blessings from what is written: הנה כי כן יברך גבר — כי יברך גבר, for יברך is written deficient in vav. Therefore they instituted to say מודים, since it means משתחוים, as it is written regarding Naaman: והשתחויתי לה׳ אלהיך, and Jonathan translated: ואודיתי קדם ה׳ אלהך. Nevertheless, we say מודים and not משתחוים, because מודים in gematria equals one hundred — to say that anyone who says מודים properly is as though he fulfilled one hundred blessings. That is, he bows until all the joints of the spine are compressed, or until he sees an issar opposite his heart, and bends like a rod and straightens like a snake, and intends to say 'we bow to You,' as is stated in the Yerushalmi: Rabbi Bun said, 'From my days I never intended...' and 'I hold it as a virtue for my head, for when I reach מודים it bends on its own.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:53.226332542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}